---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="Eligibility, scoring, disclosure classification, and corrections."
>
  <article class="shell prose-page">
    <h1>Methodology</h1>

    <section id="eligibility">
      <h2>Eligibility</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The primary arXiv category begins with <code>math.</code>.</li>
        <li>
          The paper or arXiv metadata explicitly discloses author use of AI or
          an LLM.
        </li>
        <li>A reviewer verifies the disclosure.</li>
        <li>The exact quotation and location are recorded.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="score">
      <h2>Score</h2>
      <div
        class="formula"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Slop Factor equals M times the sum of P, six T, four L, four Q, three C, two D, E over four, R over ten, and two A."
      >
        Slop Factor = M × (P + 6T + 4L + 4Q + 3C + 2D + E/4 + R/10 + 2A)
      </div>
      <dl class="definition-list">
        <div><dt>P</dt><dd>Pages</dd></div>
        <div><dt>T</dt><dd>Theorems</dd></div>
        <div><dt>L</dt><dd>Lemmas</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Q</dt><dd>Propositions</dd></div>
        <div><dt>C</dt><dd>Corollaries</dd></div>
        <div><dt>D</dt><dd>Definitions</dd></div>
        <div><dt>E</dt><dd>Displayed equations</dd></div>
        <div><dt>R</dt><dd>Bibliography entries</dd></div>
        <div><dt>A</dt><dd>Appendix pages</dd></div>
        <div><dt>M</dt><dd>Disclosure multiplier</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section id="classification">
      <h2>Multipliers</h2>
      <div class="method-table">
        <table>
          <thead
            ><tr><th scope="col">M</th><th scope="col">Disclosed role</th></tr
            ></thead
          >
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1</td><td>Proofreading, grammar, or spelling</td></tr>
            <tr><td>1</td><td>Translation</td></tr>
            <tr><td>1</td><td>Formatting or typesetting</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2</td><td>Literature search</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2</td><td>Citation assistance</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2</td><td>Brainstorming or outlining</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2</td><td>Code generation, completion, or debugging</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3</td><td>Computational experiments or data processing</td></tr>
            <tr><td>4</td><td>Rewriting existing author-written text</td></tr>
            <tr><td>5</td><td>Drafting limited passages</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6</td><td>Suggesting mathematical examples or conjectures</td></tr>
            <tr><td>7</td><td>Substantial text generation</td></tr>
            <tr><td>8</td><td>Proof ideas or individual proof-step assistance</td></tr>
            <tr><td>9</td><td>Drafting a complete proof for author revision</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10</td><td>Substantial proof generation</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10</td><td>Substantial mathematical content or result generation</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The highest applicable multiplier is used. Intermediate values require a
        recorded rationale.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="counting">
      <h2>Counts</h2>
      <p>
        Source files are preferred for theorem-like environments, displayed
        equations, and bibliography entries. PDF text is the fallback. Each
        record stores the method and any count notes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="corrections">
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections to quotations, classifications, counts, metadata, and
        versions are reviewed through version-controlled changes. Inclusion
        records a disclosure; it is not criticism of the paper or its authors.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
